  "term": "overactivity",
  "definition": "Overactivity, in this mental health context, means heightened autonomic bodily activity that can accompany anxiety. It refers to physical signs such as butterflies in the stomach, indigestion, palpitations, hyperventilation, sweating, flushing, tremor, headache, or frequent urination.",
